}
note right of AudioOutputDevice
  One QAudioSink at a time — playTestTone()
  and startStreaming() (issue #70, push-mode
  for a live call's remote audio) share it,
  starting either stops whatever was playing
  before it. finished() isn't emitted for a
  streaming session's idle-between-writes
  state, only for playTestTone()'s buffer
  actually draining.
end note
AudioOutputDevice --> "0..1" QAudioSink : owns (unique_ptr)
AudioOutputDevice ..> QAudioDevice : uses

class AudioInputDevice {
  +start(device: QAudioDevice)
  +stop()
  +isCapturing() : bool
  .. signals ..
  +levelChanged(level: float)
  +pcmDataAvailable(data: QByteArray, format: QAudioFormat)
  +errorOccurred(message: QString)
  -startCapture(device: QAudioDevice)
  -readAvailableData()
  -{static} computeLevel(pcmData: QByteArray, format: QAudioFormat) : float
}
note right of AudioInputDevice
  start() calls QCoreApplication::checkPermission()/
  requestPermission() (QMicrophonePermission) before
  startCapture() — Qt never shows the macOS prompt on
  its own for an Undetermined status.

  pcmDataAvailable() (issue #70) carries the same
  raw buffer levelChanged() computes from — lets
  CallManager forward real microphone audio into a
  call without this class knowing about calls at all.
end note
