CameraDevice --> "0..1" QCamera : owns (unique_ptr)
CameraDevice *-- QMediaCaptureSession : owns
CameraDevice *-- QVideoSink : owns
CameraDevice ..> QCameraDevice : uses
note right of CameraDevice
  start() calls QCoreApplication::checkPermission()/
  requestPermission() (QCameraPermission) before
  camera_->start() — same requestPermission() gap as
  AudioInputDevice.

  QMediaCaptureSession only supports one video sink at
  a time — CameraDevice owns that one sink itself and
  re-emits every frame via frameAvailable() (issue #72)
  instead of exposing the session for a widget to attach
  directly. Lets both the settings preview widget (fed
  manually via videoSink()->setVideoFrame()) and a call's
  outgoing video (CallVideoTrackSource::pushFrame())
  share the one camera capture — same single-owner
  pattern as AudioInputDevice/AudioOutputDevice.
end note

