}
CallVideoTrackSource --|> WebrtcAdaptedVideoTrackSource
CallVideoTrackSource ..> QVideoFrame : converts (via QImage, libyuv::ARGBToI420)
note right of CallVideoTrackSource
  Video-side counterpart to CallAudioDeviceModule
  (issue #72) — Qt Multimedia has no built-in way to
  push frames into a webrtc::VideoTrackSourceInterface.
  pushFrame() converts each QVideoFrame to I420 via
  QImage as an intermediate step (simpler and more
  robust than hand-parsing every native camera pixel
  format, at the cost of an extra conversion pass),
  then calls the inherited OnFrame() — AdaptedVideoTrackSource
  handles per-sink resolution adaptation (AdaptFrame())
  and all sink registration.

  WebRTC's own build disables RTTI, so its exported
  classes (like AdaptedVideoTrackSource) have a vtable
  but no typeinfo in libwebrtc.a — any RTTI-enabled code
  defining a derived class's out-of-line virtuals, or
  instantiating webrtc::RefCountedObject<T> for one via
  make_ref_counted<T>(), needs typeinfo referencing the
  base's, which doesn't exist. Root CMakeLists.txt
  disables RTTI project-wide (nothing here uses
  dynamic_cast/typeid) rather than chasing this file by
  file as more WebRTC-derived classes are added.

  setIsScreencast() (issue #112): CallManager shares
  this one source between camera video and screen
  share rather than creating a second track, flipping
  the hint here whenever it switches which one is
  active. isScreencast_ is std::atomic<bool> — set from
  the GUI thread, read by is_screencast() from whatever
  WebRTC thread queries it.
end note

